From 91fd541144d37ee301d714ae24ac8ffda3800197 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rafe Walker <45343084+rafe-walker@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 11:42:29 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 10/14] fix(core): return pods_exec output when the command
 exits non-zero

When the executed command exited with a non-zero code, pods_exec
discarded everything it had captured and returned only "failed to exec
in pod <p> in namespace <ns>: command terminated with exit code N". The
output that explains the failure (kubectl exec prints both streams and
exits with the same code) was lost.

execOutput.finish now keeps stdout and stderr when the stream error is
an exit-code error (k8s.io/utils/exec ExitError), and the tool returns
the error followed by the captured streams, each under a `--- stdout ---`
or `--- stderr ---` label. The result is still an error. Other stream
errors, such as a broken connection, drop the partial buffers as before
(TestOtherStreamErrorDropsBuffers is unchanged), and the
max_backend_response_bytes cut is unchanged.

Returning stderr alongside stdout on success (it is dropped when stdout
is non-empty) is a deliberate choice from #1174 and is not changed here.

The SPDY exec test helper gains StreamContext.WriteExitCode, which
sends the kubelet's NonZeroExitCode status, so the MCP test can exercise
the path end to end.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
